              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": ": Choose one of the creature’s spell-like abilities, subject to the restrictions described in this feat. The creature can use the chosen spell-like ability as a quickened spell-like ability three times per day (or less, if the ability is normally usable only once or twice per day)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "node_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "Using a quickened spell-like ability is a swift action that does not provoke an attack of opportunity. The creature can perform another action—including the use of another spell-like ability (but not another swift action)—in the same round that it uses a quickened spell-like ability. The creature may use only one quickened spell-like ability per round."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "node_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "The creature can only select a spell-like ability duplicating a spell with a level less than or equal to 1/2 its caster level (round down) – 4. For a summary, see the table below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "node_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "A spell-like ability that duplicates a spell with a casting time greater than 1 full round cannot be quickened."
            }
          ]
        },
